# history — real-world examples

## Top 10 most-used commands

```sh
history | awk '{CMD[$2]++;count++;}END { for (a in CMD)print CMD[a] " " CMD[a]/count*100 "% " a;}' | grep -v "./" | column -c3 -s " " -t | sort -nr | nl | head -n10
```

## Keyboard shortcuts (readline)

```text
alt-<    # move to beginning of history
alt->    # move to end of history
ctrl-r   # reverse incremental search
alt-p    # reverse search, non-incremental
alt-n    # forward search, non-incremental
ctrl-o   # execute current history item and advance to the next
```

## Bang (!) expansions

```text
!!        # repeat the last command
!N        # repeat history item number N
!string   # repeat last command starting with string
!?strg    # repeat last command containing strg
!$        # last argument of previous command:  ls /home  ->  ls -l !$
```

## Reuse arguments from earlier commands

```sh
touch /home/david/Desktop/1.txt
cp /home/david/Desktop/1.txt /home/david/Downloads
echo "1st Argument is : !^"      # first argument of last command
echo "2nd Argument is : !cp:2"   # 2nd argument of the last cp in history
# !*  = all arguments; also works as !xyz:*
```

## Execute past history items by keyword

```sh
ls /home > /dev/null
ls -l /home/david/ > /dev/null
ls -Al /home/david/Downloads > /dev/null

!ls        # runs the most recent ls ...
!ls -l     # ... narrowed by prefix
!ls -Al
```

## Everyday homelab moves

```sh
sudo !!                            # re-run last command with sudo
HISTTIMEFORMAT="%F %T " history | tail -20   # timestamps on recent commands
history -d 1234                    # delete one entry (that mistyped password)
history | grep 'zypper in'         # what did I install on this box?
```
